      "content": "i get that it sounds metaphysical, but the physical reaction in the studio was too consistent to be just \"psychological.\" the glass didn't just shake, it changed pitch in sympathy with the sub-harmonics. if the air density is actually shifting, there has to be a mathematical bridge between the acoustic wave and the bio-electric field of the person in the room. if we look at it through the lens of cymatics and bio-resonance, isn't it possible there's a specific frequency threshold where neuro-electrical resistance drops? can we try to model a theoretical wave pattern that would interact with the human prefrontal cortex's electromagnetic field?",
      "source": "evaluator"
